Analyze this {language} code for resource leaks and blocking-async defects.

Source file:
{source}

Already reported by mechanical pattern analysis — do NOT report these again:
{known_findings}

Detect:
- Handles (files, sockets, connections, readers, streams) not closed on every path
- Cleanup that only runs on the success path, skipped when an exception is thrown
- defer, finally or using placed inside a loop so cleanup piles up until the function exits
- Async work started and never awaited, so failures are lost and ordering is undefined
- Blocking waits on asynchronous work that can deadlock a captured context
- Timers, subscriptions, watchers or event handlers never cancelled or unregistered
- Connection pools, executors or clients created per call instead of reused
- Goroutines, threads or tasks that can outlive their caller with no cancellation signal

Return a JSON array of findings. Each finding:
{{
  "leak_type": "UNCLOSED_HANDLE|CLEANUP_ON_SUCCESS_ONLY|DEFER_IN_LOOP|UNAWAITED_TASK|BLOCKING_WAIT|UNCANCELLED_TIMER|PER_CALL_CLIENT|UNBOUNDED_WORKER|OTHER",
  "line": <line number>,
  "severity": "high|medium|low",
  "description": "one sentence describing the specific leak and how it is reached",
  "fix": "concrete fix suggestion"
}}

Return [] if no issues found. Return ONLY the JSON array, no prose.
